","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucagrementieri/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucagrementieri/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucagrementieri/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucagrementieri/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lucagrementieri","id":20520836,"login":"lucagrementieri","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNTIwODM2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucagrementieri/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucagrementieri/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucagrementieri/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucagrementieri/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucagrementieri/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucagrementieri","user_view_type":"public"},"author_association":"NONE","body":"The export of `return_11_almost_zeros ` generates the textual IR\r\n```\r\nENTRY main.5 {\r\n  Arg_0.1 = f32[2,2]{1,0} parameter(0)\r\n  Arg_1.2 = f32[2,2]{1,0} parameter(1)\r\n  constant.3 = f32[11]{0} constant({...})\r\n  ROOT tuple.4 = (f32[11]{0}) tuple(constant.3)\r\n}\r\n```\r\nso it's clear that the program cannot know the values in `constant.3`.\r\n\r\nReading the source code of `https://github.com/google/jax/blob/main/examples/jax_cpp/main.cc` I discovered that the textual representation is there only for debug purposes, so I tried the binary `pb` output and the results are the expected ones.\r\n\r\nTherefore, I suppose **the HLO textual representation should never be used in production environment**.","created_at":"2022-05-23T09:00:09Z","event":"commented","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/10588#issuecomment-1134387469","id":1134387469,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/10588","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc5DnWEN","performed_via_github_ap